<!doctype html><html><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>Student Evidence Template</title><link rel="stylesheet" href="/styles.css"></head><body><header><a class="brand" href="/">STEM Journey</a><nav><a href="/teacher">Teacher</a><a href="/student">Student</a><a href="/rubric">Rubric</a><a href="/student-evidence-template">Evidence Template</a></nav></header><main><section class="pagehead"><span class="pill">Student Evidence Integration</span><h1><%=template.templateName%></h1><p>This is the basic structure I would use inside Student Evidence. It separates the engineering journey into seven evidence sections.</p><div class="actions"><a class="button" href="/download/student-evidence-template.json">Download JSON</a><a class="button secondary" href="/download/student-evidence-template.md">Download Markdown</a></div></section><section class="lesson-grid"><% template.suggestedFields.forEach(s=>{ %><article class="lesson"><h2><%=s.section%></h2><p><%=s.prompt%></p><h3>Suggested evidence</h3><ul><% s.evidence.forEach(e=>{ %><li><%=e%></li><% }) %></ul></article><% }) %></section><section class="panel"><h2>Suggested Student Evidence data structure</h2><p>The JSON endpoint is available at <code>/api/student-evidence-template</code>. This makes it straightforward to map the template into a database-backed Student Evidence assignment/workbook later.</p></section></main><footer>Year 9 STEM • Farting Bin Engineering Challenge • 7 weeks</footer><script src="/app.js"></script></body></html>